# pnpm

- Set `"type": "module"` in each package. Set `"private": true` in each
  package that you do not publish.
- In a monorepo, link a workspace package with `workspace:*`. Put a shared
  dependency in the catalog of `pnpm-workspace.yaml`, and refer to it with
  `catalog:`. Run the fan-out scripts from the root `package.json`.
- The supply-chain settings are in the seed `pnpm-workspace.yaml`
  (`minimumReleaseAge`, `strictDepBuilds`, `trustPolicy` and
  `blockExoticSubdeps`).
- `pnpm audit` is advisory only.<% if has .all "osv-scanner" %> The gate for a known vulnerability is
  `code:sec:30-osv-scanner`.<% end %>
- `pnpm outdated` is a report only. It fails when it finds an old package, so
  it is not a gate.
- The install, upgrade, range and lockfile rules are in the bootstrap section
  of `CLAUDE.md`.

Read `references/conventions.md` for the conventions, and
`references/local.md` for the own rules of this repository.
